[Opening "Benko Gambit Accepted: Modern Variation"]

{Benko Gambit Accepted: Modern Variation. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. e3 axb5 {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. Bxb5 g6 7. a4 Ba6 8. Nc3 ! Bg7 {Here the exchange is tempting and wrong: trading the good bishop leaves the dark squares bare.} (8... c4 Rb1 Bxb5 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Nge2 O-O 10. O-O d6 11. Ra3 Bxb5 ?! 12. Nxb5 Na6 13. Nec3 Qd7 14. h3 Rfb8 15. e4 Ne8 16. b3 Nec7 17. Ra2 Rb7 18. Re2 Rc8 19. Bb2 Rcb8 20. Rfe1 Nxb5 21. Nxb5 Nc7 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Nxc7 Qxc7 24. Qa1+ Kg8 25. e5 Qd8 26. h4 h5 27. Re4 Rxb3 28. exd6 Qxd6 29. Rxe7 Qxe7 30. Rxe7 Rb1+ 31. Re1 Rxa1 32. Rxa1 c4 33. Kf1 Rb2 34. Ra3 Rb3 35. Ra1 Rb2 36. g3 c3 37. Rc1 Ra2 38. Rxc3 Rxa4 39. Ke2 Kf8 40. Kd3 Ke7 41. Rc7+ Kf6 42. f4 Ra3+ 43. Rc3 Ra4 44. Rc7 Ra3+ 45. Rc3 Ra4 46. Rc4 Ra3+ 47. Kd4 Rxg3 48. Ra4 {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} Rh3 1/2-1/2
